# traces/MANIFEST.sha256 - digests of the generated trace sets (SW §5.6). The data is not in git:
# every set is regenerated byte-identically by its regen.sh from fixed seeds (`traces/<set>/regen.sh
# build/dev`). A set's digest is the sha256 of `sha256sum` over its files (regen.sh and Python caches
# excluded) in byte-order path order; check one with
#   cd traces && find <set> -type f ! -name regen.sh ! -path '*/__pycache__/*' -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
# The digests are those of the dev host: the generator draws some random inputs through libm
# (normal deviates, the ROPE constants), so another libm may give different bytes.
# A frozen reference set goes into git once the ISA is frozen for the RTL (after the M6 RTL).
# 2026-10-30: m2, gen and m3 regenerated without SPM_STALE (every SPM line an op reads is
# written earlier in its trace; 41 traces changed: m2 13, gen 5, m3 23); vu, at, ctrl byte-identical.
# 2026-10-31: CTL_ID[7:0] 1 (version reset, docs/design/06-software-verification.md §6.9): every set's
# meta.json config.ctl_id 23810 -> 23809 (1326 files); every other byte identical (each set's digest
# with that one field normalized equals the old set's).
# 2026-10-31: trace_stats.py removed from traces/m3: m3 is 5104 files with a new digest (no trace byte
# changed; its old digest covered trace_stats.py).
